  "details": "Instances should be able to filter out certain content. NSFW avatar's aren't/shouldn't allowed in public instances.\n\nRegular public instances that are accessible to all age ranges should have a filter that blocks adult suggestive sexual content by default. \n\nGroup owners should be able to filter what avatars (based on their tags) are allowed in the instance before creating one\n\nThese features are more aligned with Meta, Google, and Apple ToS/Guidelines on adult content (included in moderated user generated content rules) and can help the younger users to not be exposed to that type of content\n\nRemember guys, this is a 13+ game, not an 18+ game and users even younger than 13 (thanks to quest support) are all over the platform and are going to instances not appropriate for them. We don't want another SonicOwO or TechGangster moment do we",
